(BWIZA JEWELS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(From one bracelet to a new way of thinking about accessories) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(PITCH DOCUMENT) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Prepared for Nazli Tech School) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2026) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The idea started with a bracelet.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I did not start Bwiza Jewels because I wanted to make another bracelet. I started by asking) Tj T*
(a simpler question: can something small, beautiful and made from natural materials carry) Tj T*
(more value than just its appearance?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(That question led me to the Umwenya concept and to a bamboo prototype. The first product is) Tj T*
(a bracelet, but the idea has already grown beyond it. I see a future where the same thinking) Tj T*
(can create earrings, necklaces, bands, beaded pieces, aromatized jewelry, personalized gifts) Tj T*
(and other accessories made from bamboo, organic beads and other organic materials.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The bracelet is the beginning of Bwiza Jewels, not the finish line.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(What makes Bwiza Jewels different) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The current prototype brings together qualities that are usually treated separately. It is) Tj T*
(cultural, aesthetic, natural and potentially functional. The bamboo gives us a starting) Tj T*
(material; the design gives it identity; and the business model gives it a reason to exist) Tj T*
(beyond a one-time souvenir purchase.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A one-of-a-kind feel: the handmade nature of the product gives each piece room for character) Tj T*
(and variation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Cultural value: designs can tell a Rwandan story instead of looking like a generic souvenir.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Sustainability: the current concept targets around 90% biodegradability, depending on the) Tj T*
(final materials and finishing used.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Function: some bracelet designs can be developed with mosquito-repellent properties for) Tj T*
(outdoor settings, subject to proper testing and validation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Choice: multiple designs allow the product to serve different tastes, ages and occasions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Who is it for?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Tourists are an important market, but they are not the whole market. Bwiza Jewels is) Tj T*
(intended for people who want to wear, give or keep something that feels connected to Rwanda) Tj T*
(and to a more natural way of making accessories.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
